! Legal Reference System

A structured system for organizing, categorizing, and prioritizing legal information.

!! Core Features

* ''Hierarchical Organization'' - Organize references by area of law, jurisdiction, and topic
* ''Priority Levels'' - Mark references as Critical, High, Medium, or Low priority
* ''Status Tracking'' - Track whether information is Current, Under Review, or Outdated
* ''Cross-References'' - Link related statutes, cases, and concepts
* ''Quick Filtering'' - Find information by priority, category, or status

!! Reference Types

|!Type |!Tag |!Description |
|Statutes |`Statute` |Legislative enactments and codes |
|Regulations |`Regulation` |Administrative rules and regulations |
|Case Law |`CaseLaw` |Judicial decisions and precedents |
|Concepts |`Concept` |Legal principles and doctrines |
|Procedures |`Procedure` |Procedural rules and requirements |
|Forms |`Form` |Standard forms and documents |

!! Priority System

|!Level |!Tag |!Use For |
|Critical |`P1-Critical` |Must-know, frequently referenced |
|High |`P2-High` |Important, regularly needed |
|Medium |`P3-Medium` |Useful, occasionally referenced |
|Low |`P4-Low` |Background, rarely needed |

